(LST2-57 — `and` joins any number of `each` clauses in one sentence, and
 the action runs once per element of the Cartesian product, ROW-MAJOR:
 the leftmost clause is the outermost loop. The manual's own two-clause
 and three-clause examples, plus a four-clause one to show "any number"
 is not two or three.
 Also covers: LST2-58 (row-major ordering — read the first column of the
 pair output: 1,1,2,2), LST2-59 (the 2x2 example), LST2-60 (the 2x2x2
 triple grid: a list and two ranges, 8 calls).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-57.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1-10
   1-20
   2-10
   2-20
   1/1/7
   1/1/8
   1/2/7
   1/2/8
   2/1/7
   2/1/8
   2/2/7
   2/2/8
   1346
   1356
   2346
   2356
)
To pair of a number called left and a number called right.
  print "{left}-{right}".

To triple of a number called one and a number called two and a number called three.
  print "{one}/{two}/{three}".

To quad of a number called one and a number called two and a number called three and a number called four.
  print "{one}{two}{three}{four}".

'pair' of each x from [1, 2] and each y from [10, 20].
'triple' of each first from [1, 2] and each second from 1 to 2 and each third from 7 to 8.
'quad' of each a1 from [1, 2] and each a2 from [3] and each a3 from 4 to 5 and each a4 from [6].
